## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical transfer learning on small data, calibration awareness, and a simple data-collection loop.

## Key Concepts

- Transfer learning with lightweight nets
- Data augmentation for small datasets
- Probability calibration (temperature scaling)
- Active/incremental labeling
- Evaluation: accuracy and calibration metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: load pretrained MobileNetV2, replace head, train on 2k images
const model = loadPretrained('MobileNetV2');
model.detachHead();
model.addHead(5);
model.freezeLayers(['conv1','conv2']);
model.compile({lr: 1e-4, loss: 'categoricalCrossentropy', optimizer:'adam'});
model.fit(dataset, {epochs: 5, augment: true});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this with a simple active-learning loop?
- What failure modes could undermine calibration on unseen classes?

## Why This Is Asked

This question adds a new angle: streaming, frame-based defect scoring with label delay and strict latency on CPU, challenging beginners to justify simple online models.

## Key Concepts

- Online learning with partial_fit or incremental updates
- Lightweight preprocessing, calibration, drift monitoring
- Latency validation, retraining cadence, evaluation metrics (AUROC, calibration)

## Code Example

```javascript
